### G.8 Checking the checks

```text
{{include ../results/mutants.txt}}
```

Two of the bugs (PENABLE asserted in the setup phase, and PSEL dropped in the setup phase) are caught *only* by an assertion. The
functional testbench can't see a setup-phase violation, because the slave model tolerates it. One (B14, read data captured without the
PREADY qualifier) is an equivalent mutant: the value presented with RVALID at the end is unchanged.

### G.9 Simulation commands and tools

```bash
make check      # lint, 8 seeds, coverage
make baseline   # as-found RTL vs the same testbench
make mutants    # injected bugs
```

You need Verilator 5.020, Python 3 and make, plus Yosys and OpenSTA for section H.

